>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheutz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Sirot</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Joly</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Forestier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevalence and characterization of Shiga toxin-producing <italic>Escherichia coli </italic>isolated from cattle, food, and children during a one-year prospective study in France</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>1023</fpage><lpage>1031</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10698990</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nishikawa</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hase</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogasawa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheasty</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Willshaw</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tatsumi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yasukawa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phage typing and DNA-based comparison of strains of enterohemorrhagic <italic>Escherichia coli </italic>O157 from apparently sporadic infections in Osaka City, Japan, 1996</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>140</fpage><lpage>143</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Werber</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fruth</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchholz</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Prager</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name>